WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.512
While Emperor Wen of Sui was on the throne, he reorganized the government and required his officials to be honest and clean.

00:00:04.862 --> 00:00:08.246
He personally chose officials who were capable and honest.

00:00:08.596 --> 00:00:13.948
He cut expenses and encouraged farming, until the storehouses were piled full of grain.

00:00:14.298 --> 00:00:18.378
Singing as they worked, the farmers carried the grain into the storehouses.

00:00:18.728 --> 00:00:24.560
The people lived and worked in peace, the markets bustled, and the country grew stronger and stronger.

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:29.422
People came and went on the streets, and laughter was everywhere.

00:00:29.772 --> 00:00:34.644
The ministers reported to the emperor the good harvests and good news from every region.

00:00:34.994 --> 00:00:38.546
Hearing this, the emperor's face broke into a smile.

00:00:38.896 --> 00:00:44.848
Emperor Wen himself lived very simply, and he is famous in history as a frugal emperor.

00:00:45.198 --> 00:00:48.486
In his three meals a day, he never wasted anything.

00:00:48.836 --> 00:00:54.620
This period of stability and prosperity was called by later generations the Kaihuang Reign.

00:00:54.970 --> 00:00:58.882
The Kaihuang Reign became a golden age praised by later generations.

